From: wine-thumbs <wine-thumbs@localhost>
Date: Fri, 18 Sep 2026 16:19:26 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] comdlg32: Send toolbar control messages to the toolbar.

IDC_TOOLBAR has the same control id as IDOK, so SendDlgItemMessage() delivered TB_CHECKBUTTON and TB_ENABLEBUTTON from the shell view to the Open button and the current view was never shown as checked.
---
 dlls/comdlg32/filedlgbrowser.c | 7 ++++++-
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/dlls/comdlg32/filedlgbrowser.c b/dlls/comdlg32/filedlgbrowser.c
index b00951aa..18e13e49 100644
--- a/dlls/comdlg32/filedlgbrowser.c
+++ b/dlls/comdlg32/filedlgbrowser.c
@@ -568,8 +568,13 @@ static HRESULT WINAPI IShellBrowserImpl_SendControlMsg(IShellBrowser *iface,
     switch (id)
     {
       case FCW_TOOLBAR:
-        lres = SendDlgItemMessageA( This->hwndOwner, IDC_TOOLBAR, uMsg, wParam, lParam);
+      {
+        FileOpenDlgInfos *info = get_filedlg_infoptr(This->hwndOwner);
+
+        /* not SendDlgItemMessage(): IDC_TOOLBAR has the same control id as IDOK */
+        lres = info ? SendMessageA(info->DlgInfos.hwndTB, uMsg, wParam, lParam) : 0;
 	break;
+      }
       default:
         FIXME("ctrl id: %x\n", id);
         return E_NOTIMPL;
